Model differences (not conformance bugs):

  ic_ref (py) is the simple, non-floating reference core. It returned a
  different result from the IC32 family on 3 workload(s):
    tetration 2^^3, tetration 2^^4, tetration 2^^4
  [2mIts failure mode is worth naming: on these it does not error or hang, it
  returns a residual superposition (e.g. `(s (s &81{a,b}))`) that reads back
  as a smaller Church numeral -- a silently wrong answer, not a crash.[0m

